[gd_scene load_steps=12 format=3]

; The Book form of the windmill: the giant of the mills.
;
; Reference: docs/reference/venture_of_montiel_concept_sheet.jpg
;
; A gaunt, nine-metre man. The arms are far too long and end in tattered
; mill sails; the head is the millstone. He is a mill read as a man, and
; not a monster: tired, workmanlike, silent.
;
; Low-poly and flat: boxes and cylinders, warm ochre skin, an olive
; cloth belt, dirty canvas. The whole thing is under 400 triangles.

